#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382833 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d228b638-d4d7-5016-bf8d-0f56d5c4fadc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437454} {:answer/id #uuid "95914e2c-927b-55a2-922e-4d9800a2f38d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437455}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d228b638-d4d7-5016-bf8d-0f56d5c4fadc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437454} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b934add-e755-50b4-b067-100e72fc3b58" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438756} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bd1d98c-7ae9-55ca-9482-d88b90b0af24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437456} {:answer/id #uuid "e43b1943-3654-567b-9fed-68e4254f3b7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437457}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e43b1943-3654-567b-9fed-68e4254f3b7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437457} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6ddf4cd-c05f-5097-8310-bbb48f377de3" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438757} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e686502-6511-5a87-9141-3f040b14bb72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437458} {:answer/id #uuid "d0bb29aa-53cb-587d-8e87-04375c2d7a7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0bb29aa-53cb-587d-8e87-04375c2d7a7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437459} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8779a01-b29f-51f0-ab0b-183634a90544" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the positive $z$-direction." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438758} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0077624-dbc3-55a6-9c6d-142323470d70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437460} {:answer/id #uuid "3165d50d-3b7d-5943-9785-4266dd0bd54a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437461}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0077624-dbc3-55a6-9c6d-142323470d70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437460} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bdf6bee-a19c-5f09-acb1-0c8cf50d5033" :answer-field/key "$F$ is irrotational" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438759}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b44da0aa-9add-572b-86e2-310e134b6864" :question/math-academy-id "q-105664" :question/problem "![](images/56/5643e87bfb5dfb5c29750f48abffe2443bf656901d74a47a0aa39bddfd0c1590.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has a curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n![](images/86/86aee33cdfa96ac0a61468cc9657e791e399f31c024cdbc3a932193dc897d534.png)\n\nIf $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$ is true, whereas statement $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would rotate clockwise. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement “$\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the positive $z$-direction” is true. Using our right hand, if we wrap our fingers in the direction of rotation (counterclockwise), our thumb will point away from the screen. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F$ also points away from the screen, in the direction of increasing $z.$\n\n- Statement “$F$ is irrotational” is false. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not irrotational.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$; “$\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the positive $z$-direction” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382840 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbe322f2-3c81-5a3f-8384-a79b47c4192c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437494} {:answer/id #uuid "cd9d57fd-6acd-56c1-9f2e-b83a1aa501a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437495}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd9d57fd-6acd-56c1-9f2e-b83a1aa501a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437495} :answer-field/id #uuid "3898a42c-a0be-50b6-8124-860e6bfc10bd" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438776} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ebb3d1f-b473-5ff0-99dc-159e666e7930" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437496} {:answer/id #uuid "f0f04e94-0931-5901-b36f-4cf0aefffcb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437497}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ebb3d1f-b473-5ff0-99dc-159e666e7930" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437496} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f5874c9-61e8-5f41-9f79-2b146b618ffd" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438777} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d37dd19-280c-5e67-ae16-cb2d1a8d8768" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437498} {:answer/id #uuid "82315627-af21-5603-83df-7fa71a175af5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d37dd19-280c-5e67-ae16-cb2d1a8d8768" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437498} :answer-field/id #uuid "87749995-78bc-517b-80a4-3ef44008acb3" :answer-field/key "$F$ is not irrotational" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438778} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e6a54cb-d3b8-527e-8166-9d17d4c66cfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437500} {:answer/id #uuid "f7668637-64a8-52ae-aa22-7ac35611bf2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e6a54cb-d3b8-527e-8166-9d17d4c66cfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437500} :answer-field/id #uuid "b01a01c4-08c1-5b79-8565-85e0e916e53a" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the negative $z$-direction." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438779}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "73b73866-28ec-57e7-b02e-d1bd053c3918" :question/math-academy-id "q-105693" :question/problem "![](images/10/10a9960200e87e1b7b8a38789d5f70f29e48ad1f0a6e2913713da90c532eca6e.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n![](images/59/594106633e422d24b9fea113d24fb6367fdef5ac52724931860e4163e33ce992.png)\n\nMoreover, if $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ is true, whereas statement $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$ is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would not rotate. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- Statements “$F$ is not irrotational” and “$\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the negative $z$-direction” are false. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F=0,$ the vector field $F$ is irrotational. And, since $\\text{curl}\\,F=0,$ it points in neither the positive nor the negative $z$-direction.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382847 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09e2916c-4330-5317-9940-8bd81420d877" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+2\\,j+3\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382849} {:answer/id #uuid "8313169e-da67-5084-89b9-6de60b1b433e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\,j+2\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382850} {:answer/id #uuid "add6679c-6145-570a-9b5b-d58274c5f26f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\,i-3\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382851} {:answer/id #uuid "64005279-cd6a-55f0-b1a4-4699a29fb345" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,i-j-k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382852} {:answer/id #uuid "d12556cf-9684-53a7-a211-1d901f057185" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "j-6\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382853}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64005279-cd6a-55f0-b1a4-4699a29fb345" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,i-j-k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382852} :answer-field/id #uuid "768eb6e6-1159-5455-954f-6daa92d3afde" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382848}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "27a8e275-9fb8-5aa1-b8f3-46200f4c3126" :question/math-academy-id "q-105698" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,i+y{z}^{2}\\,j+(x-z)\\,k.$ Evaluate $∇\\times F$ at the point  $(2,-1,3).$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the curl of $F$ is the vector field given by\n\n$$\ncurl\\,F=∇\\times F=\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y) & y{z}^{2} & (x-z)\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x-z)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(y{z}^{2})]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x-z)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y))]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y{z}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y))]k \\\\  & =(0-2yz)i-(1-0)j+(0-\\frac{1}{x+y})k \\\\  & =-2yz\\,i-j-\\frac{1}{x+y}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{curl}\\,F$ at the point $(2,-1,3),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\text{curl}\\,F)(2,-1,3) & =-2(-1)(3)\\,i-j-\\frac{1}{2+(-1)}\\,k \\\\  & =6\\,i-j-k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383034 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2a14eda-ccab-5f7f-a719-20929206c183" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383036} {:answer/id #uuid "7f5fbc0f-62fd-51ae-9453-284b6e551213" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383037} {:answer/id #uuid "a64f1af0-be8c-5a44-a9cc-2fba5bb44234" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383038} {:answer/id #uuid "78cbd39b-453a-54ac-94ad-3b0b9c0fae93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383039} {:answer/id #uuid "2a33efaf-3611-56e4-a949-ec2d696d451d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383040}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a33efaf-3611-56e4-a949-ec2d696d451d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383040} :answer-field/id #uuid "a90f1f2e-6bea-5afb-916e-20d455797ede" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383035}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1ef0a7a3-f12b-51cf-8356-485327cebc47" :question/math-academy-id "q-123175" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,i+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-y)\\,j.$ \nEvaluate $∇\\cdot F$ at the point $(0,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives  of the components of $F$ all exist, then the divergence of $F$ is the scalar field given by\n\n$$\n\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F=\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y))+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x+y}+\\frac{(-1)}{x-y} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{div}\\,F$ at the point $(0,-1),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\cdot F)(0,-1) & =-\\frac{2(-1)}{{0}^{2}-(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{(-2)}{(-1)} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383041 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60937b06-70ea-5c5a-b823-3f7549956fb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383043} {:answer/id #uuid "7b44972d-191a-5729-ae14-a89b1f4b0c42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383044} {:answer/id #uuid "bc975208-2acd-5024-a13d-ca18e4d8b16f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383045} {:answer/id #uuid "6d3e76e5-a29e-5d75-b27c-e2d8dfd0de01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383046} {:answer/id #uuid "8e46db48-04cb-5171-923b-8c8d70b490f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e46db48-04cb-5171-923b-8c8d70b490f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383047} :answer-field/id #uuid "81a2e1fd-a1e3-5cc4-a1da-9e8f0ebbe408" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383042}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9c8a3eea-616a-5c49-bb08-64624b7ee7d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-123192" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F={x}^{2}yz\\,i+x{y}^{2}z\\,j+xy{z}^{2}\\,k.$ \nEvaluate $∇\\cdot F$ at the point $(1,2,2).$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the divergence of $F$ is the scalar field given by\n\n$$\n\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F=\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}+\\frac{∂R}{∂z}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}+\\frac{∂R}{∂z} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}yz)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{y}^{2}z)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =2xyz+2xyz+2xyz \\\\  & =6xyz.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{div}\\,F$ at the point $(1,2,2),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\cdot F)(1,2,2) & =6(1)(2)(2) \\\\  & =6\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383048 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e78342e-7073-5996-b8d2-29a251917883" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437704} {:answer/id #uuid "1d04d934-dcdb-526f-b570-2dbcc6fce5a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437705}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d04d934-dcdb-526f-b570-2dbcc6fce5a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437705} :answer-field/id #uuid "b474b307-7652-5024-93ce-3d6d184d1386" :answer-field/key "$F=x{y}^{2}\\,i+{x}^{2}y\\,j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438881} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65dc72a9-ac06-5f1a-bf28-b0607daf1e58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437706} {:answer/id #uuid "a136b1c8-384b-51aa-80e4-6450fc364d0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65dc72a9-ac06-5f1a-bf28-b0607daf1e58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437706} :answer-field/id #uuid "70c7e673-aa45-56c5-83bc-18fb8c69889f" :answer-field/key "$G=2x\\,i-3(x+y)\\,j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438882} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0467504c-f5ba-5c65-b935-abce7630a7ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437708} {:answer/id #uuid "fab9a31b-ee2c-52cf-8167-c9659890b4a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437709}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0467504c-f5ba-5c65-b935-abce7630a7ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437708} :answer-field/id #uuid "8654b8c1-2a6a-54eb-b934-803e7b9c7856" :answer-field/key "$H={e}^{x-y}\\,i+{e}^{y-x}\\,j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438883}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7f81692c-bc38-55e0-9228-b9c2fd15506d" :question/math-academy-id "q-123866" :question/problem "Which of the following vector fields are conservative on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let $F(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j$ be a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2},$ where $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first-order partial derivatives everywhere on $D.$ Then, we have the following theorem:\n\n$F$ *is conservative if and only if $\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}$ everywhere on $D.$*\n\nNote that for each of our functions, $D={R}^{2}.$ With this in mind, let's check each of the vector fields.\n\n- For the vector field $F,$ we have $P=x{y}^{2}$ and $Q={x}^{2}y.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2xy,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=2xy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are continuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $F$ is conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- For the vector field $G,$ we have $P=2x$ and $Q=-3(x+y).$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are not equal, we conclude that $G$ is not conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- For the vector field $H,$ we have $P={e}^{x-y}$ and $Q={e}^{y-x}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-{e}^{x-y},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=-{e}^{y-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are not equal, we conclude that $H$ is not conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $F=x{y}^{2}\\,i+{x}^{2}y\\,j$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383055 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd9d3890-e5fa-57a3-9137-eeba2c84a593" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383057} {:answer/id #uuid "d2e62bfe-1108-53de-82a5-a03533c4f994" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383058} {:answer/id #uuid "d05e703d-f6df-5364-a2c7-03adc5fdd414" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383059} {:answer/id #uuid "31c18c30-748a-5d6c-9a1a-4722fa3a251d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383060} {:answer/id #uuid "70ad12cb-bd4a-5ceb-a9c2-f1f68db1330e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383061}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31c18c30-748a-5d6c-9a1a-4722fa3a251d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383060} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bcb7611-75f0-57b9-8afb-f4a5ccb4b065" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383056}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f2d723a2-0f08-5c17-a7db-01dafeefa476" :question/math-academy-id "q-123999" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F=a\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-y)\\,i+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-y)+1)\\,j$ on ${R}^{2}$, where $a$ is a constant. Given that $F$ is conservative, find the value of $a.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $F(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j$ be a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2},$ where $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first-order partial derivatives everywhere on $D.$ Then, we have the following theorem:\n\n$F$ *is conservative if and only if $\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}$ everywhere on $D.$*\n\nFor the vector field $F,$ the domain $D={R}^{2},$ and we have \n\n$$\nP=a\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-y),\\,Q=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-y)+1.\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-a\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-y),\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-y).\n$$\n\nIt's clear that the partial derivatives exist and are continuous on ${R}^{2}.$ Equating the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-a\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-y) & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-y) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-y)+a\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-y) & =0 \\\\ (3+a)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-y) & =0 \\\\ 3+a & =0 \\\\ a & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $a=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383062 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69cdb73c-68f9-51c3-a494-dbe4266db912" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383064} {:answer/id #uuid "417e54d2-9717-5a97-a672-bbd2ccb8aafb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383065} {:answer/id #uuid "f4cc8f77-f135-588f-ab23-c3509ab33e20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383066} {:answer/id #uuid "2f9778f5-bd6a-5d4b-81d4-8238d7ae5689" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383067} {:answer/id #uuid "6247fb45-a096-58a2-8ab7-eac0357ef0e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383068}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4cc8f77-f135-588f-ab23-c3509ab33e20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383066} :answer-field/id #uuid "1329f6f4-d27c-52fa-b484-d7367ccdea8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383063}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c88bce86-de64-567d-8976-da96551577ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-126520" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=(x+{y}^{2})\\,i+y\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)\\,j.$ Evaluate the scalar curl of $F$ at the point $(0,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the *scalar* curl of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1))-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy}{{x}^{2}+1}-2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the scalar curl at the point $(0,-1),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})}_{(0,-1)} & =\\frac{2(0)(-1)}{{0}^{2}+1}-2(-1) \\\\  & =0+2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383069 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60ac814a-bd23-5ee0-b4f1-9f60f6f92a04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383071} {:answer/id #uuid "413bc497-4dc9-517b-955f-ff234af7121f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383072} {:answer/id #uuid "68aee1b1-ce3f-5ba3-8aee-10ef06e824b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383073} {:answer/id #uuid "b4a78035-db24-5d4f-b02e-a5266dbde465" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383074} {:answer/id #uuid "3fb908f3-12e2-51fd-82ab-4f09ca5fad8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60ac814a-bd23-5ee0-b4f1-9f60f6f92a04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383071} :answer-field/id #uuid "83fe23ea-1458-55ab-bb2d-e5ba77ca30b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383070}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a595714d-0237-5554-9973-668e9384b87c" :question/math-academy-id "q-126527" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=(x-{y}^{2})\\,i+({y}^{3}-x)\\,j.$ Evaluate the scalar curl of $F$ at the point $(-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the *scalar* curl of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{3}-x)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x-{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-1-(-2y) \\\\  & =2y-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the scalar curl at the point $(-1,1),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})}_{(-1,1)} & =2(1)-1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383076 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be488c31-9256-566c-b32a-08e6c160f22c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383078} {:answer/id #uuid "f7488729-2ee4-53c3-8133-c6ecbdfd35b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383079} {:answer/id #uuid "53b1ed95-0584-576a-b16d-faf84c6c5497" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383080} {:answer/id #uuid "045cf962-a0e3-5f5d-9614-af24c41f8a68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383081} {:answer/id #uuid "4063a276-ab18-5a28-835e-27da301a0497" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "045cf962-a0e3-5f5d-9614-af24c41f8a68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383081} :answer-field/id #uuid "b22a1cc1-84ab-59a2-be59-cc57b115de95" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383077}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8cde4f56-4a8b-58dd-9183-074bcd7df016" :question/math-academy-id "q-126537" :question/problem "Given that $F(x,y)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,i+(2x+3y)\\,j,$ what is the scalar curl of $F?$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the *scalar* curl of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x+3y)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) \\\\  & =2-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383244 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63333efd-d822-5e6a-8874-2684764a6d34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383246} {:answer/id #uuid "4a7079b8-ca98-5f78-a0b6-63d45fdc3398" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383247} {:answer/id #uuid "b10571cd-8ad7-5a71-9cc7-86e1745517db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383248} {:answer/id #uuid "d598bc98-2e8d-5dd9-8b10-90cffd05991d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383249} {:answer/id #uuid "3e6fa43e-0e0d-55cd-ba9c-8dc1b7762999" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383250}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63333efd-d822-5e6a-8874-2684764a6d34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383246} :answer-field/id #uuid "047c58de-3cf8-57f5-9db0-76ef729a4311" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383245}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c49fed94-087c-5bc2-a0ce-0e5ce4848c8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-131173" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F=x{e}^{y}\\,i+xy{e}^{y}\\,j.$ \nEvaluate $∇\\cdot F$ at the point $(2,0).$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the divergence of $F$ is the scalar field given by\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot F=\\text{div}\\,F=\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{e}^{y})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy{e}^{y}) \\\\  & ={e}^{y}+x{e}^{y}+xy{e}^{y}. \\\\  & =(1+x+xy){e}^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{div}\\,F$ at the point $(2,0),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\cdot F)(2,0) & =(1+2+2(0)){e}^{0} \\\\  & =3{e}^{0} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383251 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86fc3b2f-e528-5aa6-b7af-f6ac8563fdab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383253} {:answer/id #uuid "e54145e9-4574-5349-ab5f-74b95bdfc80e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383254} {:answer/id #uuid "c500d2b6-da10-5778-a6c4-74d2a9185191" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383255} {:answer/id #uuid "0fe21f00-818c-554f-8500-ea894f1c8d6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383256} {:answer/id #uuid "945ed3b6-1c5c-5567-b83c-3afdc324a0d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383257}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fe21f00-818c-554f-8500-ea894f1c8d6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383256} :answer-field/id #uuid "4feb22a8-b9e6-59d8-a756-c12f2d26d5cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383252}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "59443564-6ec5-5ec7-a934-99dc847cb69c" :question/math-academy-id "q-131174" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F=x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,i+y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,j.$ \nEvaluate $∇\\cdot F$ at the point $(3,4).$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the divergence of $F$ is the scalar field given by\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot F=\\text{div}\\,F=\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}+\\frac{{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{div}\\,F$ at the point $(3,4),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\cdot F)(3,4) & =3\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{9+16} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383258 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62fd903f-e649-5428-9a2f-4c1aa5f6c22b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+2\\,j+3\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383260} {:answer/id #uuid "52796190-4740-539c-8e75-a6ad7f819b37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,j-2\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383261} {:answer/id #uuid "f7c8091c-bce1-56d7-80ae-658179937524" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-i+2\\,j-3\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383262} {:answer/id #uuid "8f933e4b-13c9-5280-a21e-056a60d49045" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3y\\,i+2x\\,j-z\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383263} {:answer/id #uuid "befb4236-3c4e-5e5d-85d6-2649a0ebfcac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383264}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "befb4236-3c4e-5e5d-85d6-2649a0ebfcac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383264} :answer-field/id #uuid "607af23d-3f74-5452-a712-45b9778ac8e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383259}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2c28fbe5-df41-51e5-b4b7-2d1414f882b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-131338" :question/problem "Given that $F(x,y,z)=x\\,i+2y\\,j+3z\\,k,$ what is $\\text{curl}\\,F?$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the curl of $F$ is the vector field given by\n\n$$\ncurl\\,F=∇\\times F=\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ x & 2y & 3z\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3z)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2y)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3z)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x)]k \\\\  & =(0-0)\\,i-(0-0)\\,j+(0-0)\\,k \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383265 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21985218-40b7-5d8e-a7c4-b8fb22c45c38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,i+\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383267} {:answer/id #uuid "f15f6c5b-022c-5634-b2a2-a72ef3b790e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,j-3\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383268} {:answer/id #uuid "81841eb6-fef1-55ac-961c-991a42be278b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\,i-2\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383269} {:answer/id #uuid "9fa83d83-20ef-5c72-8eb3-bcef1e295d9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,i+\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383270} {:answer/id #uuid "932f3e67-8dcb-55ab-a9a7-82af9923a07a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\,j+\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383271}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21985218-40b7-5d8e-a7c4-b8fb22c45c38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,i+\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383267} :answer-field/id #uuid "2056a6e2-aef3-52c4-ab48-744cca8dde53" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383266}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "119c787c-79ba-5ec1-aa8b-ef2fb283c3d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-131340" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F={x}^{2}\\,i+xz\\,j+{z}^{2}\\,k.$ Evaluate $∇\\times F$ at the point  $(-2,-3,1).$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the curl of $F$ is the vector field given by\n\n$$\ncurl\\,F=∇\\times F=\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ {x}^{2} & xz & {z}^{2}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}({z}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xz)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}({z}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xz)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2})]k \\\\  & =(0-x)i-(0-0)j+(z-0)k \\\\  & =-x\\,i+z\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{curl}\\,F$ at the point $(-2,-3,1),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\text{curl}\\,F)(-2,-3,1) & =-(-2)\\,i+(1)\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,i+\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383272 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7851f0f-e955-50b1-bb5f-692cb729d280" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+j+3\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383274} {:answer/id #uuid "33eecef9-292f-5109-a112-0c1000c6dc0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+\\,j+6\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383275} {:answer/id #uuid "7edc97b5-9983-5cf8-b6da-26436232bb79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+3\\,j+2\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383276} {:answer/id #uuid "ba79d3eb-8cfe-5884-a1ff-8d90a2ca3b33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "j+6\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383277} {:answer/id #uuid "fc89b77e-7dfe-566f-87d4-07f18b28028f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+3\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383278}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33eecef9-292f-5109-a112-0c1000c6dc0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+\\,j+6\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383275} :answer-field/id #uuid "067c58e5-4d4b-51d3-bf82-b6a875039aed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383273}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c75d4d2c-54c4-5038-ab10-417305bd22e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-131341" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F=(2xy+2z)\\,i+({y}^{2}+1)\\,j+(x+y)\\,k.$ Evaluate $∇\\times F$ at the point  $(-3,0,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the curl of $F$ is the vector field given by\n\n$$\ncurl\\,F=∇\\times F=\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ 2xy+2z & {y}^{2}+1 & x+y\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x+y)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({y}^{2}+1)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+y)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2xy+2z)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}+1)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy+2z)]k \\\\  & =(1-0)i-(1-2)j+(0-2x)k \\\\  & =\\,i+j-2x\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{curl}\\,F$ at the point $(-3,0,-1),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\text{curl}\\,F)(-3,0,-1) & =i+\\,j-2(-3)\\,k \\\\  & =\\,i+\\,j+6\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383607 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97cfef0b-b2e9-52d1-81b0-399192df2eb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383609} {:answer/id #uuid "4bd4c4de-e1e5-5ff6-83aa-88f43410589b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t){e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383610} {:answer/id #uuid "a4d046f0-8479-5ddd-8e29-9cf04c57ccd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t){e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383611} {:answer/id #uuid "6cf412ac-5ff2-5717-972e-75f25275ddc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+1){e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383612} {:answer/id #uuid "9e75a459-147f-5daa-8fd7-55841122ff55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383613}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4bd4c4de-e1e5-5ff6-83aa-88f43410589b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t){e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383610} :answer-field/id #uuid "614acb07-1733-5745-addd-2f741b4bd7c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383608}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5274ee67-b6e6-57da-a682-d2ddd4bf1256" :question/math-academy-id "q-170669" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)={e}^{2y-x},x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ and $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-{e}^{2y-x},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2{e}^{2y-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =-{e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =2{e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =-{e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+2{e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t){e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383614 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8172957c-8ded-58d3-9a23-800391f6abc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383616} {:answer/id #uuid "65fc28e8-01f1-5779-81a2-95006d854621" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{s}-2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383617} {:answer/id #uuid "78f76e21-a29b-5ac4-bef0-5e96cc36b301" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{s}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383618} {:answer/id #uuid "1650585c-4f5b-5c09-98dc-1b8f36155d98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{s}+2+t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383619} {:answer/id #uuid "9d243851-27bb-5ff4-9d66-8de5b61c5110" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{s}+t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383620}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78f76e21-a29b-5ac4-bef0-5e96cc36b301" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{s}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383618} :answer-field/id #uuid "a31244f4-c1a2-50a4-adcb-bc5510fae670" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383615}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "04777d40-e9e1-5da3-94ee-34ffd4874f77" :question/math-academy-id "q-170674" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=z-x-y,$ where $x={e}^{s}+t,$ $y=s+1$ and $z=1-t-s.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/be/be6afcdd0ad9ae0d7ef377c4918442a64e1186c90c25e27ec6c224d816a602fd.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-1,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-1,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & ={e}^{s}, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =1, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂s} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =(-1)\\cdot {e}^{s}+(-1)\\cdot 1+(1)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-{e}^{s}-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385363 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e42d90a-97cf-5414-b80d-82a4862b83de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2s{cos}^{2}⁡t-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385365} {:answer/id #uuid "016496f9-039d-53a6-96db-cf3960e6a193" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2s{sin}^{2}⁡t-2{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385366} {:answer/id #uuid "cb6f4593-e298-5f84-b3e8-cd2d86629bbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{s}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t+4t{sin}^{2}⁡s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385367} {:answer/id #uuid "b99ddb71-4211-5aa0-a805-5281aabf9bee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{s}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385368} {:answer/id #uuid "a78b674e-3f6a-5922-89c6-75ee6f89da98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-4{t}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385369}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "016496f9-039d-53a6-96db-cf3960e6a193" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2s{sin}^{2}⁡t-2{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385366} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c5d0091-d440-5a1e-b574-7e1631c61ea7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385364}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "66bc23d2-d72e-5919-9b3d-d85b675dd732" :question/math-academy-id "q-37201" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-2{y}^{2},$ where $x=s\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$ and $y=t\\operatorname{sin}⁡s.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/21/21cec766fe72965697304ef4288ffb2b090ddfca179210165dbcfd42ec490b27.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t)$ and $y=y(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-4y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =2s\\operatorname{sin}⁡t, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =-4t\\operatorname{sin}⁡s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡t, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =t\\operatorname{cos}⁡s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s} \\\\  & =(2s\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+(-4t\\operatorname{sin}⁡s)(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡s) \\\\  & =2s{sin}^{2}⁡t-4{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s\\operatorname{cos}⁡s \\\\  & =2s{sin}^{2}⁡t-2{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385370 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "894ca471-2dd4-5d40-b36a-8da27b160d4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385372} {:answer/id #uuid "a0652b0f-d1a7-5fb6-a24a-41d904eaf606" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385373} {:answer/id #uuid "290a2a7e-ad92-516f-ae90-67ba3132c946" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385374} {:answer/id #uuid "5ad83d4e-e307-5e90-9e4f-cc60c72f71d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385375} {:answer/id #uuid "10e3eea0-e64b-5459-8cc2-03bcb5ecde36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385376}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ad83d4e-e307-5e90-9e4f-cc60c72f71d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385375} :answer-field/id #uuid "98ca2715-a0aa-5460-b75b-4a47465638ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385371}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7b9407c6-12a8-5179-a6fb-edc61bbc79bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-37208" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{y}^{2}z,$ where $x=3t,$ $y=t-s$ and $z=2st.$ Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂t}=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t+{c}_{1}s{t}^{2}+{c}_{2}{s}^{2}t+{c}_{3}{s}^{3},\n$$\n\nfind the value of ${c}_{1}+{c}_{2}+{c}_{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/b5/b593a1b60fe8c1aef2c5c229ff426db350e6296b9ecb767494283f0fa3342072.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2yz,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}={y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =2(t-s)(2st)=4s{t}^{2}-4{s}^{2}t, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =(t-s)^{2}={t}^{2}-2st+{s}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂t} & =3, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂t} & =1, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂t} & =2s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂t} & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t)\\cdot 3+(4s{t}^{2}-4{s}^{2}t)\\cdot 1+({t}^{2}-2st+{s}^{2})\\cdot 2s \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t+4s{t}^{2}-4{s}^{2}t+2s{t}^{2}-4{s}^{2}t+2{s}^{3} \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t+6s{t}^{2}-8{s}^{2}t+2{s}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${c}_{1}=6,$ ${c}_{2}=-8$ and ${c}_{3}=2,$ and therefore\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}+{c}_{3}=6+(-8)+2=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385415 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1b52115-29e3-5e95-b508-73c86b6c7161" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z{e}^{xz}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-\\frac{1}{z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385417} {:answer/id #uuid "fcb2c780-ae80-5c02-98ec-088e06656270" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z{e}^{xz}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385418} {:answer/id #uuid "c23d4ba1-b4af-5e1d-8241-74ca34e9132f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z{e}^{xz}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-{e}^{xy}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+\\frac{1}{z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385419} {:answer/id #uuid "6137c52a-00ed-5c54-9df7-7714367d3018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xz{e}^{xz}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\frac{1}{yz}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385420} {:answer/id #uuid "c82109a8-b32c-5783-b93b-9700fb963ae0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z{e}^{xz}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\frac{1}{z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385421}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c82109a8-b32c-5783-b93b-9700fb963ae0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z{e}^{xz}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\frac{1}{z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385421} :answer-field/id #uuid "4373b52e-949a-57c9-b4c4-b3ece34fb1b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385416}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "09702191-588f-54f0-a2ed-482de5d4de8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-41837" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F=⟨{e}^{xz}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y,\\,0,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡yz⟩.$ Find $\\text{div}\\,F.$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the divergence of $F$ is the scalar field given by\n\n$$\n\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F=\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}+\\frac{∂R}{∂z}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}+\\frac{∂R}{∂z} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{xz}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(0)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡yz) \\\\  & =z{e}^{xz}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\frac{1}{z}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385824 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "010a1725-78d9-5ef6-976d-66b572c1b87d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ts({t}^{2}-3ts+2{s}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385826} {:answer/id #uuid "3a12b2ee-d263-5ffd-96bf-c7a89479c594" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s{t}^{2}(s-2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385827} {:answer/id #uuid "cd01d3dd-a324-5561-83a5-466a5fba3616" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t({s}^{2}+s+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385828} {:answer/id #uuid "bc3eb310-caaa-5a1e-9eea-e12deb4203bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ts(1+ts)(1-st)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385829} {:answer/id #uuid "39c971fc-9574-59c2-93dc-706cf5f69912" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t{s}^{2}(2s-3t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39c971fc-9574-59c2-93dc-706cf5f69912" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t{s}^{2}(2s-3t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385830} :answer-field/id #uuid "722f5fc1-8625-5de3-b976-ddcdf5183ff0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385825}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cddd99f6-007e-52c0-bac7-f496a002a8cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-94748" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)=y{x}^{2},$ where $x=ts$ and $y=s-t.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂t}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/11/118759b163a4410f66d5855d7b7b1fd9c2ee4be585e778a759997036bd95f765.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t)$ and $y=y(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2xy,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =2(ts)(s-t)=2t{s}^{2}-2s{t}^{2}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =(ts)^{2}={t}^{2}{s}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂t} & =s, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂t} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂t} \\\\  & =(2t{s}^{2}-2s{t}^{2})(s)+({t}^{2}{s}^{2})(-1) \\\\  & =2t{s}^{3}-2{s}^{2}{t}^{2}-{t}^{2}{s}^{2} \\\\  & =2t{s}^{3}-3{t}^{2}{s}^{2} \\\\  & =t{s}^{2}(2s-3t).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385838 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "247ee7d0-904c-5d01-8297-06a98015037c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{s}}){e}^{\\sqrt{s}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385840} {:answer/id #uuid "7cec0dc1-33bb-5f04-a034-05527df9b19d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1+s){e}^{\\sqrt{s}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385841} {:answer/id #uuid "323b91bd-668a-507d-8f83-8a04b4f2b115" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2+\\sqrt{s}){e}^{\\sqrt{s}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385842} {:answer/id #uuid "ffd6bb8a-7411-5765-b787-90052e6b40f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{s}}){e}^{\\sqrt{s}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385843} {:answer/id #uuid "0fbb05f2-b967-534b-9feb-494c22d63500" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1+\\frac{\\sqrt{s}}{2}){e}^{\\sqrt{s}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fbb05f2-b967-534b-9feb-494c22d63500" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1+\\frac{\\sqrt{s}}{2}){e}^{\\sqrt{s}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385844} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f70704d-2718-514e-b670-1b5ed75416ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385839}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c583feca-7024-59b3-b46e-988493997541" :question/math-academy-id "q-95083" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=y{e}^{x},$ $x=\\sqrt{s}$ and $y=s,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s}$ for $s>0.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/7e/7e5b5001794ecdf2c9b9e9102f334a63d2c59bc6f7511c2eb7fa358fc94cb0c5.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $s,$ where $x=x(s)$ and $y=y(s),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=y{e}^{x},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =s{e}^{\\sqrt{s}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & ={e}^{\\sqrt{s}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{s}},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s} \\\\  & =s{e}^{\\sqrt{s}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{s}}+{e}^{\\sqrt{s}}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{s}}{2}{e}^{\\sqrt{s}}+{e}^{\\sqrt{s}} \\\\  & =(1+\\frac{\\sqrt{s}}{2}){e}^{\\sqrt{s}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385913 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f34066d-e5f3-59d1-b457-19e4e5363985" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385915} {:answer/id #uuid "6559cd7c-65d2-5d2c-b543-974d47b3bed8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e\\,i+2j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385916} {:answer/id #uuid "4e73f922-b725-5fdc-85a9-5d438d7e19cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i-2j+2e\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385917} {:answer/id #uuid "448ec01e-63d9-5985-be70-04517cbccf2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i-2e\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385918} {:answer/id #uuid "68728130-3e32-5eba-b606-02d0d2544d2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-i+e\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e73f922-b725-5fdc-85a9-5d438d7e19cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i-2j+2e\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385917} :answer-field/id #uuid "93fef15b-13ac-5973-a47f-908616ae5cb3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385914}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aeed6089-b923-5c58-9f18-b9dd1c803098" :question/math-academy-id "q-98894" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F=xy{e}^{z}\\,j+yz{e}^{x}\\,k.$ Evaluate $∇\\times F$ at the point $(0,2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3},$ and the first partial derivatives exist, then the curl of $F$ is the vector field on ${R}^{3}$ defined by\n\n$$\ncurl\\,F=∇\\times F=\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ 0 & xy{e}^{z} & yz{e}^{x}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(yz{e}^{x})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy{e}^{z})]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(yz{e}^{x})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(0)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy{e}^{z})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(0)]k \\\\  & =(z{e}^{x}-xy{e}^{z})i-(yz{e}^{x}-0)j+(y{e}^{z}-0)k \\\\  & =(z{e}^{x}-xy{e}^{z})\\,i-yz{e}^{x}\\,j+y{e}^{z}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{curl}\\,F$ at the point $(0,2,1),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\text{curl}\\,F)(0,2,1) & =(1\\cdot {e}^{0}-0\\cdot 2\\cdot {e}^{1})\\,i-2\\cdot 1\\cdot {e}^{0}\\,j+2\\cdot {e}^{1}\\,k \\\\  & =i-2j+2e\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387222 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d59160e7-9169-5e83-a5c4-ad0518caff28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/21/2132ac0140fb0b96a876fd04a1069d6922662c72d4d8f4b8880eacae458f8181.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387224} {:answer/id #uuid "d5e66ef4-c389-503c-adac-bf6a7d3d4bc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fe/fefa684ba6cc6b2e8060c8b0860295177bade694786439317d6cee3d8cf51da8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387225} {:answer/id #uuid "1a97f507-5b03-5608-9bf1-7d0e5956f463" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/55/559ffda45a088810dcaa81628b8767bfedc64ca7f6b7ebd82aebdb2ed4a7ba00.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387226} {:answer/id #uuid "e78dff93-70e1-5457-996d-4e768112af8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/45/459b65c41ef9535d55703a64f3c9e4bfe9ffd9263a6a0f5dbf68405fb22c347d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387227} {:answer/id #uuid "0f013635-08f3-5ce8-b2d1-e6ffd2a329b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9a/9a20235e26590dbc6ddc5bdaaaa5dd484f5caf02e510bfabf2139ed7add5fa2d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387228}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a97f507-5b03-5608-9bf1-7d0e5956f463" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/55/559ffda45a088810dcaa81628b8767bfedc64ca7f6b7ebd82aebdb2ed4a7ba00.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387226} :answer-field/id #uuid "6702c2d4-7e00-59d1-8dcc-92a8c2e4e69d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387223}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "57d2166f-4843-548f-9e93-704a19813c47" :question/math-academy-id "q-122554" :question/problem "Determine which of the following shaded regions depicts the domain of the vector field $F$ on ${R}^{2},$ given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}\\,i+\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{x-y}\\,j\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The function $F$ can be expressed in terms of its components $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y)$ as\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j,\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}},\\,Q(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{x-y}.\n$$\n\nWe first find the domain of each component function. Then, we compute their intersection to find the domain of $F:$\n\n- The function $P(x,y)$ is defined when the expression under the radical is positive. So, to find the domain, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n3-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}>0\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<3.\n$$\n\nThis defines the region ${D}_{1},$ which is the interior of a circle of radius $\\sqrt{3},$ as shown below:\n\n![](images/f9/f9c3a22a56839165bfd6c3b05f78ca25053553532063192836d0332d2b070436.png)\n\n- The function $Q(x,y)$ is defined everywhere other than when the denominator vanishes. To find where the denominator vanishes, we set it equal to zero and solve:\n\n$$\nx-y=0\\,⟹\\,x=y.\n$$\n\nThis defines the region ${D}_{1},$ which is the entire plane ${R}^{2}$ with the line $y=x$ removed:\n\n![](images/a1/a1ef93cc90bdd59b922723c2c2aa2bd670b43e416923892c9db53b36ac6b7e57.png)\n\nFinally, the domain $D$ of $F$ is given by ${D}_{1}\\cap {D}_{2},$ shown below.\n\n![](images/f7/f70cab5ec58e63e1751faa65b575a20da748b3e8ee90cffac8f1f3b029bbbd79.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387437 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3809196-0e72-568a-acb4-8f1806b011f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d1/d1cec5ea2da4a0b5f141bb24b4addc797defbc48e76cdfdbfab3a303e348b8cc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387439} {:answer/id #uuid "d44a46da-960a-5000-b573-28968c62249a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bc/bcb2b08bab14ce74347d37a0e896451750db0203ab830b835a83de6b7a81b61d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387440} {:answer/id #uuid "a8c8555e-f76d-58d2-98de-66b72a2089cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/02/02b248ea373f295fa4dbad215eba4c211ef18548dca4a56d57cb3f15424ad501.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387441} {:answer/id #uuid "6dbecde8-5a29-5731-8756-dcd4a93b4487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/09/097262c9e70a68d3a7ae1b1186bed57cefd7b99b0af2215d4ce6b08a086f90c6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387442} {:answer/id #uuid "63870ff1-4a2f-5845-b126-b062e8aa81ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c4/c477137fe47dc3f0475f44658117545da3dae94f18e3bf2ce897d2a89fad2a37.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387443}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8c8555e-f76d-58d2-98de-66b72a2089cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/02/02b248ea373f295fa4dbad215eba4c211ef18548dca4a56d57cb3f15424ad501.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387441} :answer-field/id #uuid "533eaf8b-e6a9-5c0c-825d-2916631bb54e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387438}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5a8d7579-5453-54bf-bdf9-b20277da40a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-123783" :question/problem "Determine the graph of the following parametrically defined curve:\n\n$$\nx=1-2t,\\,y=t,\\,-3\\le t\\le 3\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to create a table of values and then sketch the curve. First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x=1-2t.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $7$ | $5$ | $3$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-3$ | $-5$ |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y=t.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $7$ | $5$ | $3$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-3$ | $-5$ |\n| $y$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](images/ef/ef5f33b74b59b5a62fd8670a8feb6487b01a97aed4a44a098a576d10d891bd68.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387444 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de89a225-5b69-58e8-af20-8b469da68382" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/06/06e9f6dca9a52ea97101e691426a98bf9c3fff46226b613f51948a0b6d5c21d8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387446} {:answer/id #uuid "99620a74-235b-56d5-bc5f-7705bb0e7c2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2f/2f7ae8161271a68f71c08c6d6b05a562e7f41aacbbeec6a703c1d84088ac2e52.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387447} {:answer/id #uuid "d63ecbf4-09df-5e02-a7fb-98c5d6badf76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/cb/cb247068f321f4cda099913d632e1d4a55679b98780a200394aa325f9a04235a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387448} {:answer/id #uuid "546faf1d-37e4-50b3-b6ca-3c10b31000ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6e/6e937a9e8e8fa7ebf3476a798c9922c846c823897d764f174e6cfb0f9cdbdd12.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387449} {:answer/id #uuid "a7e46b14-46e0-5e71-9844-29886a6b5cc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/07/07a91c29e0b24b90570e1a656d8823a1ea3427863ec1e7e7ed80543869bbb87e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387450}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d63ecbf4-09df-5e02-a7fb-98c5d6badf76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/cb/cb247068f321f4cda099913d632e1d4a55679b98780a200394aa325f9a04235a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387448} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6dc38a6-c20e-5f76-8686-fb64abd39bd1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387445}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d90f041c-edf1-58a7-aee4-ec1e2efc48d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-123785" :question/problem "Determine the graph of the following parametrically defined curve:\n\n$$\nx=5-{t}^{2},\\,y={t}^{2}-3,\\,0\\le t\\le 3\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to create a table of values and then sketch the curve. First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x=5-{t}^{2}.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $5$ | $4$ | $1$ | $-4$ |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y={t}^{2}-3.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $5$ | $4$ | $1$ | $-4$ |\n| $y$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $1$ | $6$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](images/a3/a39e8a0c4ed269e5cb73aaedf0655d85302f3a5c3c7e91d9f5e58ebf84a82423.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387685 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "359ca0ff-973b-506e-a465-b43c34cba969" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\,{\\int }_{0}^{3}r\\,dr\\,d\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387687} {:answer/id #uuid "0ccab75f-a602-56ce-b1a3-cd10fa0dbc03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\,{\\int }_{0}^{3}{r}^{3}\\,dr\\,d\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387688} {:answer/id #uuid "c0dec30f-8c79-5a3a-acee-c51c3f82081c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{3}{r}^{3}\\,dr\\,d\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387689} {:answer/id #uuid "49ca9510-621f-51b6-90c6-5b9cbb3cdc98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{3}r\\,dr\\,d\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387690} {:answer/id #uuid "9a2f6402-c9e4-529d-b588-36204d64955a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\,{\\int }_{0}^{2}(r+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ))\\,dr\\,d\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ccab75f-a602-56ce-b1a3-cd10fa0dbc03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\,{\\int }_{0}^{3}{r}^{3}\\,dr\\,d\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387688} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bee84b5-4364-5ef7-b230-57a279a56f9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387686}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "21730a28-6e7f-5db6-af91-78ecf92baa4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-126514" :question/problem "![](images/c1/c1f8bb7ed82d345f8397ea9b01854f05f3f668acdcebf5d75ebbc5cb8de04fa6.png)\n\nConsider the path $C$ shown above. Which of the following is equivalent to the line integral \n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-{x}^{2}y)\\,dx+(x{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{y+1})\\,dy\\,?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the region $D$ and its boundary $C$ satisfy the conditions of Green's theorem:\n\n![](images/9e/9eceb8ab173995a8325fb1a8452baaa7f1071e569391e9a49b69c047d76f3b52.png)\n\nSince $P(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-{x}^{2}y$ and $Q(x,y)=x{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{y+1},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-{x}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}={y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-{x}^{2}y)\\,dx+(x{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{y+1})\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}({y}^{2}-(-{x}^{2}))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the region $D$ can be represented in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 3,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi \\}.\n$$\n\nThe change of variables formula for plane polar coordinates states that \n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our double integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}({r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\,{\\int }_{0}^{3}{r}^{3}\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387699 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01b89c47-d0b2-5264-b994-b98209bb77be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{5}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,dr\\,d\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387701} {:answer/id #uuid "2db9727e-440f-5931-aa1e-281498cdc499" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{5}{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,dr\\,d\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387702} {:answer/id #uuid "64f5a418-b56a-53fb-b2ff-23e7ac5231c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\,{\\int }_{0}^{5}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,dr\\,d\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387703} {:answer/id #uuid "c8dbfa5f-5e35-5361-b706-416c1d369242" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\,{\\int }_{0}^{5}{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,dr\\,d\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387704} {:answer/id #uuid "fe4753f6-a11c-59ab-853f-472db759de2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{5}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,dr\\,d\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387705}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe4753f6-a11c-59ab-853f-472db759de2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{5}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,dr\\,d\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387705} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddb9d9aa-d773-5af6-b8b4-ba71799f08c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387700}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b97bdd87-b8e7-5fa0-84d3-dcb91e945069" :question/math-academy-id "q-126686" :question/problem "![](images/e4/e44543ad51864a7db6b8e80b5c560a1ac773a7537573014f737451af4d1209a7.png)\n\nConsider the path $C$ shown above. Which of the following is equivalent to the line integral \n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}(x{y}^{2}-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,dx+(2{x}^{2}y-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,dy\\,?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the region $D$ and its boundary $C$ satisfy the conditions of Green's theorem:\n\n![](images/d8/d8ee02b2b7282349604dc6305c0b2be796cfdbd2937e06d089e660683a5785ad.png)\n\nSince $P(x,y)=x{y}^{2}-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and $Q(x,y)=2{x}^{2}y-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2xy-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=4xy-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}(x{y}^{2}-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,dx+(2{x}^{2}y-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(4xy-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-(2xy-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2xy\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the region $D$ can be represented in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 5,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe change of variables formula for plane polar coordinates states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our double integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2xy\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}2(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{5}2{r}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,dr\\,d\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{5}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387706 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d925ce22-07b4-5c26-811c-95dafb568817" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{4}(2r-{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,dr\\,d\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387708} {:answer/id #uuid "5dd24fe2-ec3e-58f0-a4da-38274f190bdf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{4}(2r{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }-{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,dr\\,d\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387709} {:answer/id #uuid "7c628f7d-ee25-5920-bf22-2d9af94503cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{4}(r{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }-{r}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,dr\\,d\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387710} {:answer/id #uuid "0acf37f8-41ac-5bc8-8f19-331dbeb6be67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{4}(2r-{r}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,dr\\,d\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387711} {:answer/id #uuid "974e402e-ac40-50a9-b8e9-36fbed90d028" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{4}(2r-{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,dr\\,d\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387712}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0acf37f8-41ac-5bc8-8f19-331dbeb6be67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{4}(2r-{r}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,dr\\,d\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387711} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5e912ff-c934-5812-954b-69ac3ae4ba0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387707}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a9090184-b791-5b13-8e38-15714ad9e0e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-126709" :question/problem "![](images/00/008f5dbaeb8c3c26008c49e97ed0490c444b049a991c2198399359a30b806b07.png)\n\nConsider the path $C$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y)=⟨{e}^{x/4}+x{y}^{2},\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}+2x⟩,$ which of the following is equivalent to $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr\\,?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we can rewrite our integral as \n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr={∮}_{C}({e}^{x/4}+x{y}^{2})\\,dx+({e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}+2x)\\,dy.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the region $D$ and its boundary $C$ satisfy the conditions of Green's theorem:\n\n![](images/c4/c40d9fdfd10b3be4153c9c8ea3a6302af3cf0392533767313c467bdf7dcec1d7.png)\n\nSince $P(x,y)={e}^{x/4}+x{y}^{2}$ and $Q(x,y)={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}+2x,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2xy,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}({e}^{x/4}+x{y}^{2})\\,dx+({e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}+2x)\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2-2xy)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the region $D$ can be represented in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 4,\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le 0\\}.\n$$\n\nThe change of variables formula for plane polar coordinates states that \n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our double integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(2-2xy)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}(2-2\\cdot r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{4}(2r-{r}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387803 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a2f6f5b-f063-50fd-a445-e5206861484d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(2{y}^{2}+6)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387805} {:answer/id #uuid "ca3a5b14-e539-50ca-b764-e8483d96d0a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2{y}^{2}(x+6)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387806} {:answer/id #uuid "ff2802b1-16eb-55bd-a33e-9c02fc8a176a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2x({y}^{2}+6)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387807} {:answer/id #uuid "8051d521-18c9-5506-8dd8-4404b731cd23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}({x}^{2}+12y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387808} {:answer/id #uuid "2d6e2d0e-132f-5112-af04-61afe3543d74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(2{x}^{2}+y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff2802b1-16eb-55bd-a33e-9c02fc8a176a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2x({y}^{2}+6)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387807} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7357b1f-7672-551e-bf04-066c16895432" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387804}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6b4bd86f-3707-5569-a669-abddd19a5594" :question/math-academy-id "q-127228" :question/problem "Consider the rectangle $C$ with vertices $(0,0),(3,0),(3,2),$ and $(0,2),$  traversed counterclockwise. Using the flux form of Green's theorem, express the flux of the vector field\n$F(x,y)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,i+12xy\\,j$\nthrough $C$ as a repeated integral." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j,$ and $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then the flux form of Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={∬}_{D}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich is equivalent to\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dy-Q\\,dx={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y})\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n \n\n![](images/23/23066b23aebf332921c22a0439a414ade8dffd2a270641d186da0ed0e9488821.png)\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}$ and $Q(x,y)=12xy.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=2x{y}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =12x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can express the region $D$ as a type I region as follows:\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y):0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 2\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem in flux form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}P\\,dy-Q\\,dx & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2x{y}^{2}+12x)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2x({y}^{2}+6)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
